# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Debian image's leak pass only (its Dockerfile names this file in
# LEAK_SUPPRESSIONS; Fedora's names lsan-fedora.supp). Each entry names one function in a library's
# own code, never a whole library; the image installs those libraries' debug symbols so the function
# has a name. Spec section 9 and CONTRIBUTING.md list both, with these reasons.

# SDL 3.2.10 (libsdl3-0 3.2.10+ds-1), the OpenGL fallback runs (gl-*): 10,600 bytes in 1 object.
#   SDL_calloc <- VULKAN_CreateRenderer (SDL_render_vulkan.c:4252)
#   <- SDL_CreateRendererWithProperties (SDL_render.c:1025) <- create_renderer (launcher.c)
# SDL's loop over the names in the renderer list skips SDL_DestroyRendererWithoutFreeing after a
# backend fails, so the Vulkan renderer's data, made before Vulkan failed to start, is never freed.
# Fixed upstream in libsdl-org/SDL 5622eef5a (2025-09-27), in 3.4.0 and later and in no 3.2.x release.
leak:VULKAN_CreateRenderer

# Mesa 25.0.7 (libglx-mesa0 25.0.7-2+deb13u1) with SDL 3.2.10, every OpenGL run: about 108 KB.
#   GL_CreateRenderer -> SDL_RecreateWindow -> SDL_GL_LoadLibrary -> X11_GL_LoadLibrary
#   -> X11_GL_GetVisual (x11opengl.c:688) -> glXChooseVisual -> __glXInitialize
#   -> AllocAndFetchScreenConfigs / driswCreateScreen / glx_screen_init (__glXQueryServerString,
#   glx_config_create_list)
# Mesa's GLX state for the X display, made once and not freed at exit with this pair; Fedora's SDL
# 3.4.18 and Mesa 26.2.4 are clean. No upstream report exists.
leak:__glXInitialize
